h the Universal Agent — it is never installed in the development venv and will always be missing. Do not attempt to verify it via `ls`, `import`, or `python3 -c`. Any import error referencing `universal_extension` is a false positive. For its API and usage, read the reference doc via `ue:retrieving-context`.\n\n**Extension imports** — verify every name imported from extension modules actually exists in the source:\n\n```bash\ngrep -rn \"^from exceptions import\\|^from fields\\|^from actions import\\|^from utility\" src/\n```\n\nCross-check each imported name against the corresponding source file to confirm it is defined.\n\nFix any mismatches before proceeding.\n\n## Task 5: Validate Python Syntax\n\n```bash\nfind src -name \"*.py\" -exec python -m py_compile {} \\;\n```\n\nFix any errors immediately — do NOT proceed until all files compile cleanly.\n\nCommon issues: invalid f-strings, indentation errors, non-default field after default field.\n\n> **`universal_extension` is a UAC ecosystem module bundled with the Universal Agent — it is not\n> available in the development environment and cannot be installed via pip. Any error referencing\n> `universal_extension` is a false positive. Do not attempt to install it, mock it, or treat it\n> as a missing dependency. For its API and usage, use the `ue:retrieving-context` skill to read `references/implementation_docs/universal_extension.md`.\n\n\n---\nWork Item ID: initial-1\nInput Files:\n- memory/initial-1/implementation-blueprint.md\n- extension-code/src/fields/input.py\n- extension-code/src/fields/output.py\n- extension-code/src/utility.py (or extension-code/src/utility/ if a directory)\n- extension-code/src/exceptions.py\nOutput Files:\n- Action output mapper: extension-code/src/actions/output.py\n- Actions package init: extension-code/src/actions/__init__.py\n- Action files: extension-code/src/actions/<action_name>.py (one file per action from analysis)\n"}

