2026-09-10 09:13:03 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"58bb7a0e-3319-436a-846d-f162b3a05195","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-servicenow-table-sync/58bb7a0e-3319-436a-846d-f162b3a05195.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/servicenow-table-sync","prompt_id":"dd86b2cc-755a-4b95-8d8e-cc3150655d8c","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/credentials.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/credentials.md","content":"# Credentials Handling\n\n## Overview\n\nAuthentication-related logic belongs in a dedicated class, not scattered across action functions. The class initialises the SDK or API client once at construction; all actions that need it share the same instance.\n\n---\n\n## Pattern\n\nGroup all authentication setup and API method wrappers into a single class:\n\n```python\nclass PipelineClient:\n    def __init__(self, input_data: InputFields) -> None:\n        credentials = _load_credentials(input_data.service_account_credentials.value)\n        aiplatform.init(\n            project=input_data.project_id,\n            location=input_data.region,\n            credentials=credentials,\n        )\n        self._project_id = input_data.project_id\n        self._region = input_data.region\n\n    def submit_job(self, display_name: str, template_path: str) -> PipelineJobResult:\n        ...\n\n    def get_state(self, resource_name: str) -> str:\n        ...\n\n    def cancel_job(self, resource_name: str) -> None:\n        ...\n```\n\nThe action class receives the client at construction time — no action method touches credentials fields directly:\n\n```python\nclass RunPipeline:\n    def __init__(self, input_data: InputFields) -> None:\n        self._input = input_data\n        self._client = PipelineClient(input_data)   # credentials resolved once here\n        self._output_fields = OutputFields()\n\n    def execute(self) -> ActionOutput:\n        result = self._client.submit_job(\n            display_name=self._input.display_name,\n            template_path=self._input.template_path,\n        )\n        ...\n```\n\n**Why**: Calling `aiplatform.init()` (or equivalent SDK setup) on every API call is redundant — most SDKs hold global or instance state keyed on project/region/credentials. Initialising once at construction makes the lifecycle explicit and reduces code duplication across actions.\n\n---\n\n## Credentials Must Come from UAC Credential Fields\n\nSensitive values (service accounts, API keys, tokens, passwords) **must** be sourced from `InputFields` that map to a UAC `credential` type field in the template. Never use `script` or plain-text `text` fields for secrets.\n\n```json\n// template.json — correct field type\n{\n  \"name\": \"service_account_credentials\",\n  \"type\": \"credential\",\n  \"label\": \"Service Account Credentials\",\n  \"required\": true\n}\n```\n\n```python\n# Good — Credential field; UAC masks the value in logs and task definitions\ncredentials_json = input_data.service_account_credentials.value\n\n# Bad — Script field exposes the secret as plain text in the UAC task definition\ncredentials_json = input_data.service_account_script.value\n```\n\n---\n\n## Multiple Authentication Methods\n\nWhen the target API supports more than one authentication method, branch on an auth-type selector field inside `__init__`. Keep the branching logic in one place; actions do not inspect credential fields:\n\n```python\nclass GitLabClient:\n    def __init__(self, input_data: InputFields) -> None:\n        if input_data.auth_type == \"token\":\n            self._gl = gitlab.Gitlab(\n                url=input_data.host_url,\n                private_token=input_data.access_token.value,\n            )\n        else:\n            self._gl = gitlab.Gitlab(\n                url=input_data.host_url,\n                oauth_token=input_data.oauth_token.value,\n            )\n        self._gl.auth()\n```\n\n---\n\n## Where to Put the Credentials Class\n\nFor simple integrations (one auth method, one SDK), the credentials class can live in a `credentials.py` module or as an inner utility within `utilities.py`. For extensions with complex authentication (multiple methods, token refresh, session management), create a dedicated `credentials.py`.\n","numLines":105,"startLine":1,"totalLines":105}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PMqcWM646VoyFzTTnjWkrh","duration_ms":2}

