2026-09-10 09:13:04 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"58bb7a0e-3319-436a-846d-f162b3a05195","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-servicenow-table-sync/58bb7a0e-3319-436a-846d-f162b3a05195.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/servicenow-table-sync","prompt_id":"dd86b2cc-755a-4b95-8d8e-cc3150655d8c","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/action_output.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/action_output.md","content":"# ActionOutput\n\n## Overview\n\nActionOutput is a dataclass returned by actions to control STDOUT printing and Extension Output (unv_output). Actions return this instead of ExtensionResult directly.\n\n## File: src/actions/output.py\n\n```python\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Optional, Any, Dict, List\nimport json\n\n@dataclass\nclass ActionOutput:\n    # Extension Output payload fields (go into the JSON result blob via to_dict())\n    # NOT the same as output-only template fields (task instance variables set via ui.update_output_fields())\n    resource_id: Optional[str] = None\n    resource_name: Optional[str] = None\n    details: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\n    items: Optional[List[Dict[str, Any]]] = None\n    metadata: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\n\n    # Human-readable result message — becomes status_description via\n    # build_result(status_description=action_output.message). Distinct from\n    # OutputFields.status, a bare progress label (see output_fields.md).\n    message: Optional[str] = None\n\n    # Control fields (from template Choice fields)\n    stdout_options: List[str] = None\n    output_options: List[str] = None\n\n    def print_output(self):\n        \"\"\"Print to STDOUT based on stdout_options.\"\"\"\n        # Implement printing logic\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        \"\"\"Convert to dict for Extension Output.\"\"\"\n        # Implement dict conversion\n```\n\n---\n\n## Serialization Contract\n\n`to_dict()` must follow these rules for all field types. Violating them produces Extension Output incompatible with downstream consumers.\n\n| Field type | Correct Python type | Wrong |\n|---|---|---|\n| `SingleChoice` | `str` — the chosen value as a plain string | `[\"value\"]` — never a one-element list |\n| `Integer` | `int` | `{\"value\": 0, \"min_value\": null, ...}` |\n| `Float` | `float` | `{\"value\": 0.0, ...}` |\n| `Boolean` | `bool` | `\"true\"` / `1` |\n| `errors` key | **Absent** when `exit_code == 0` | Never include `\"errors\": []` on success |\n\n```python\ndef to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    include_all = len(self.output_options) == 0\n    output = {}\n\n    # SingleChoice → plain str (not a list)\n    if self.pipeline_region:\n        output[\"pipeline_region\"] = str(self.pipeline_region)\n\n    # Integer → plain int (not a dict or str)\n    if self.retry_count is not None:\n        output[\"retry_count\"] = int(self.retry_count)\n\n    # Boolean → plain bool\n    if self.is_active is not None:\n        output[\"is_active\"] = bool(self.is_active)\n\n    # Do NOT add an 'errors' key on successful execution.\n    # extension.py populates errors only on failure — never add it here.\n\n    return output\n```\n\n## ActionOutput Fields Must Be Plain Python Types\n\n`ActionOutput` fields must be declared and populated as plain Python types (`str`, `int`, `float`, `bool`, `list`, `dict`). **Never put wrapper types from `fields.types` (`Integer`, `SingleChoice`, `Float`, `Boolean`, `Text`) directly into `ActionOutput`.**\n\nWhen populating `ActionOutput` from `InputFields`, always extract the underlying value:\n\n```python\n# Good — extract the plain value from the wrapper\nreturn ActionOutput(\n    pipeline_region=input_data.region.value,       # SingleChoice.value → str\n    retry_count=int(input_data.max_retries),        # Integer → int\n    dry_run=bool(input_data.dry_run),               # Boolean → bool\n    pipeline_state=result.state.name,               # SDK enum → str (from API response)\n)\n\n# Bad — wrapper types leak into ActionOutput; asdict() or json.dumps() will mangle them\nreturn ActionOutput(\n    pipeline_region=input_data.region,              # SingleChoice → {\"_values\": [\"us-central1\"]}\n    retry_count=input_data.max_retries,             # Integer → {\"value\": 3, \"min_value\": null, ...}\n    dry_run=input_data.dry_run,                     # Boolean → {\"value\": True}\n)\n```\n\nThe wrapper types define `__int__`, `__float__`, `__bool__`, `__str__` for use in expressions, but these do **not** auto-trigger when the object is stored in a dict and serialized to JSON. Always call `.value` or wrap with `int()` / `float()` / `bool()` explicitly.\n\n---\n\n## Usage in Actions\n\n```python\nfrom actions import ActionOutput\n\ndef create_resource(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    # Perform operation\n    resource = create(input_data.resource_name)\n\n    # Return output\n    return ActionOutput(\n        resource_metadata={\n            \"resource_id\":resource.id,\n            \"resource_name\":resource.name\n        }\n        details={\n            \"status\": \"created\",\n            \"region\": \"us-east-1\",\n            \"created_at\": timestamp\n        }\n    )\n```\n\n## STDOUT Control\n\nUsers select what to print via `stdout_options` field in template.\n\n**Fallback behavior:** Empty list = print everything\n*Only if there is no controll fields in the template, otherwise an emplty list means print nothing*\n\n```python\ndef print_output(self):\n    print_all = len(self.stdout_options) == 0\n\n    # Always print basics\n    if self.resource_id:\n        print(f\"\\nResource ID: {self.resource_id}\")\n    if self.resource_name:\n        print(f\"Resource Name: {self.resource_name}\")\n\n    # Conditional printing based on user selection\n    if (print_all or \"details\" in self.stdout_options) and self.details:\n        print(\"\\n--- Details ---\")\n        for key, value in self.details.items():\n            print(f\"  {key}: {value}\")\n\n    if (print_all or \"items\" in self.stdout_options) and self.items:\n        print(f\"\\n--- Items ({len(self.items)}) ---\")\n        for i, item in enumerate(self.items, 1):\n            print(f\"  {i}. {item}\")\n\n    if (print_all or \"metadata\" in self.stdout_options) and self.metadata:\n        print(\"\\n--- Metadata ---\")\n        for key, value in self.metadata.items():\n            print(f\"  {key}: {value}\")\n```\n\n## Extension Output Control\n\nUsers select what goes in unv_output via `output_options` field in template.\n\n**Fallback behavior:** Empty list = include everything\n*Only if there is no controll fields in the template, otherwise an emplty list means print nothing*\n\n```python\ndef to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    include_all = len(self.output_options) == 0\n    output = {}\n\n    # Always include basics\n    if self.resource_id:\n        output[\"resource_id\"] = self.resource_id\n    if self.resource_name:\n        output[\"resource_name\"] = self.resource_name\n\n    # Conditional inclusion based on user selection\n    if (include_all or \"details\" in self.output_options) and self.details:\n        output[\"details\"] = self.details\n\n    if (include_all or \"items\" in self.output_options) and self.items:\n        output[\"items\"] = self.items\n        output[\"item_count\"] = len(self.items)\n\n    if (include_all or \"metadata\" in self.output_options) and self.metadata:\n        output[\"metadata\"] = self.metadata\n\n    return output\n```\n\n## Field Customization\n\nDefine fields based on your extension's needs:\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass ActionOutput:\n    # Detailed information\n    details: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\n    properties: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\n\n    # Collections\n    items: Optional[List[Dict[str, Any]]] = None\n    warnings: Optional[List[str]] = None\n\n    # Metadata\n    metadata: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\n    statistics: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None\n\n    # Control fields\n    stdout_options: List[str] = None\n    output_options: List[str] = None\n```\n\n## Template.json Integration\n\nControl fields defined in template.json:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"stdout_options\",\n  \"type\": \"choice\",\n  \"label\": \"STDOUT Options\",\n  \"multiple_select\": true,\n  \"required\": false,\n  \"default\": [],\n  \"choices\": [\n    {\"label\": \"Details\", \"value\": \"details\"},\n    {\"label\": \"Items\", \"value\": \"items\"},\n    {\"label\": \"Metadata\", \"value\": \"metadata\"}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nActions receive these from InputFields:\n\n```python\nreturn ActionOutput(\n    resource_id=resource.id,\n    details=details,\n    stdout_options=input_data.stdout_options,\n    output_options=input_data.output_options\n)\n```\n\n## __post_init__ Pattern\n\nInitialize control fields with fallback:\n\n```python\ndef __post_init__(self):\n    \"\"\"Initialize control fields.\"\"\"\n    if self.stdout_options is None:\n        self.stdout_options = []\n    if self.output_options is None:\n        self.output_options = []\n```\n\n## Complete Example\n\n```python\n@dataclass\nclass ActionOutput:\n    resource_id: Optional[str] = None\n    items: Optional[List[Dict]] = None\n    statistics: Optional[Dict] = None\n\n    stdout_options: List[str] = None\n    output_options: List[str] = None\n\n    def __post_init__(self):\n        if self.stdout_options is None:\n            self.stdout_options = []\n        if self.output_options is None:\n            self.output_options = []\n\n    def print_output(self):\n\n        if (\"items\" in self.stdout_options) and self.items:\n            print(f\"Items: {len(self.items)}\")\n            for item in self.items[:5]:  # Show first 5\n                print(f\"  - {item['name']}\")\n\n        if (\"statistics\" in self.stdout_options) and self.statistics:\n            print(\"\\nStatistics:\")\n            for key, val in self.statistics.items():\n                print(f\"  {key}: {val}\")\n\n    def to_dict(self) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n        include_all = len(self.output_options) == 0\n        output = {}\n\n        if self.resource_id:\n            output[\"resource_id\"] = self.resource_id\n\n        if (include_all or \"items\" in self.output_options) and self.items:\n            output[\"items\"] = self.items\n            output[\"item_count\"] = len(self.items)\n\n        if (include_all or \"statistics\" in self.output_options) and self.statistics:\n            output[\"statistics\"] = self.statistics\n\n        return output\n```\n\nSee src/actions/output.py for full implementation.","numLines":310,"startLine":1,"totalLines":310}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KiYXFwzpmiVRobifiHe1yX","duration_ms":2}

