2026-09-10 09:13:09 - Received stdin data: {"session_id":"58bb7a0e-3319-436a-846d-f162b3a05195","transcript_path":"/tmp/.claude/projects/-tmp-servicenow-table-sync/58bb7a0e-3319-436a-846d-f162b3a05195.jsonl","cwd":"/tmp/servicenow-table-sync","prompt_id":"dd86b2cc-755a-4b95-8d8e-cc3150655d8c","permission_mode":"bypassPermissions","effort":{"level":"high"},"hook_event_name":"PostToolUse","tool_name":"Read","tool_input":{"file_path":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/logging.md"},"tool_response":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/tmp/iss-ue-plugin/claude/uac/ue/skills/retrieving-context/references/implementation_docs/logging.md","content":"# Logging\n\n## Overview\n\nLogging is essential for troubleshooting and debugging Universal Extensions. Use Python's logging module to provide visibility into extension execution.\n\n## Setup\n\n**Import logger at module level:**\n\n```python\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"UNV\")\n```\n\n**ALWAYS use `\"UNV\"` as the logger name** - this ensures all extension logs are captured under the Universal Extension logger hierarchy.\n\n## Logging Levels\n\n### logging.info()\nUse for major steps and important events that should be visible during normal operation:\n\n```python\nlogger.info(\"Starting resource creation\")\nlogger.info(\"Connecting to database: %s\", database_name)\nlogger.info(\"Successfully authenticated with API\")\nlogger.info(\"Completed processing %d items\", total_count)\nlogger.info(\"Action completed successfully\")\n```\n\n**When to use:**\n- Function entry for main operations\n- Connection establishment\n- Authentication success\n- Major milestones (batch processing progress)\n- Successful completion\n\n### logging.debug()\nUse for detailed diagnostic information useful during troubleshooting:\n\n```python\nlogger.debug(\"Request URL: %s\", url)\nlogger.debug(\"Request headers: %s\", headers)\nlogger.debug(\"Response status code: %d\", response.status_code)\nlogger.debug(\"Response data: %s\", response.text)\nlogger.debug(\"Query parameters: %s\", params)\nlogger.debug(\"Processing item: %s\", item_id)\n```\n\n**When to use:**\n- API request/response details\n- Query parameters and payloads\n- Intermediate values and calculations\n- Loop iterations (for debugging)\n- Configuration values\n\n### logging.warning()\nUse for recoverable issues or unexpected situations:\n\n```python\nlogger.warning(\"Retry attempt %d of %d\", attempt, max_retries)\nlogger.warning(\"Item %s skipped: missing required field\", item_id)\nlogger.warning(\"Using default value for %s\", field_name)\n```\n\n### logging.error()\nUse for errors that prevent operation but allow continuation:\n\n```python\nlogger.error(\"Failed to process item %s: %s\", item_id, str(e))\nlogger.error(\"API request failed: %s\", error_message)\n```\n\n**Note**: Errors are typically logged and then raised, not just logged.\n\n## Action Logging Patterns\n\n### Function Entry\n```python\ndef create_resource(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    \"\"\"Create a new resource.\"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Starting create_resource action\")\n    logger.debug(\"Input data: action=%s, resource_name=%s\",\n                 input_data.action, input_data.resource_name)\n```\n\n### Key Operations\n```python\n# Before API call\nlogger.info(\"Creating resource: %s\", resource_name)\nlogger.debug(\"API endpoint: %s\", endpoint_url)\nlogger.debug(\"Request payload: %s\", payload)\n\n# After API call\nlogger.info(\"Resource created successfully: %s\", resource_id)\nlogger.debug(\"API response: %s\", response_data)\n```\n\n### Loop Processing\n```python\nlogger.info(\"Processing %d items\", len(items))\n\nfor i, item in enumerate(items):\n    logger.debug(\"Processing item %d/%d: %s\", i+1, len(items), item.name)\n    # Process item...\n\nlogger.info(\"Completed processing %d items\", len(items))\n```\n\n### Function Exit\n```python\nlogger.info(\"create_resource action completed successfully\")\nlogger.debug(\"Returning resource_id=%s\", resource_id)\nreturn ActionOutput(resource_id=resource_id)\n```\n\n### Error Handling\n```python\ntry:\n    result = risky_operation()\nexcept SpecificError as e:\n    logger.error(\"Operation failed: %s\", str(e))\n    raise ExecutionError(f\"Failed to complete operation: {str(e)}\")\n```\n\n## Utility Function Logging Patterns\n\n### Database Connection\n```python\ndef connect_to_database(host: str, database: str) -> Connection:\n    \"\"\"Connect to PostgreSQL database.\"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Connecting to database: %s@%s\", database, host)\n    logger.debug(\"Connection parameters: host=%s, database=%s, port=%d\",\n                 host, database, port)\n\n    try:\n        conn = psycopg2.connect(...)\n        logger.info(\"Successfully connected to database\")\n        logger.debug(\"Connection object: %s\", conn)\n        return conn\n    except psycopg2.Error as e:\n        logger.error(\"Database connection failed: %s\", str(e))\n        raise DatabaseConnectionError(f\"Failed to connect to {database}@{host}: {str(e)}\")\n```\n\n### API Request\n```python\ndef make_api_request(url: str, method: str = \"GET\", **kwargs) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Make HTTP API request.\"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Making %s request to %s\", method, url)\n    logger.debug(\"Request parameters: %s\", kwargs)\n\n    try:\n        response = requests.request(method, url, **kwargs)\n        logger.debug(\"Response status: %d\", response.status_code)\n        logger.debug(\"Response body: %s\", response.text)\n\n        response.raise_for_status()\n        logger.info(\"API request successful\")\n        return response.json()\n    except requests.RequestException as e:\n        logger.error(\"API request failed: %s\", str(e))\n        raise APIError(f\"Request to {url} failed: {str(e)}\")\n```\n\n### CLI Command Execution\n```python\ndef execute_cli_command(binary_name: str, args: list) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Execute CLI command from vendor directory.\"\"\"\n    binary_path = VENDOR_DIR / binary_name\n    logger.info(\"Executing CLI command: %s %s\", binary_name, ' '.join(args))\n    logger.debug(\"Binary path: %s\", binary_path)\n\n    try:\n        result = subprocess.run(\n            [str(binary_path)] + args,\n            capture_output=True,\n            text=True,\n            check=True\n        )\n        logger.info(\"CLI command executed successfully\")\n        logger.debug(\"Command output: %s\", result.stdout)\n        return result.stdout\n    except subprocess.CalledProcessError as e:\n        logger.error(\"CLI command failed: %s\", e.stderr)\n        raise CLIExecutionError(f\"Command failed: {e.stderr}\")\n```\n\n## Complete Example\n\n### Action with Full Logging\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Create resource action.\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nfrom fields.input import InputFields\nfrom actions.output import ActionOutput\nfrom fields.output import OutputFields\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nfrom exceptions import ExecutionError\nfrom utility import create_resource_api, validate_resource_name\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"UNV\")\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\n\n\ndef create_resource(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    \"\"\"\n    Create a new resource.\n\n    Args:\n        input_data: Validated input fields\n\n    Returns:\n        ActionOutput with creation results\n    \"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Starting create_resource action\")\n    logger.debug(\"Input: action=%s, resource_name=%s, timeout=%s\",\n                 input_data.action,\n                 input_data.resource_name,\n                 input_data.timeout)\n\n    # Initialize output tracking\n    output_fields = OutputFields(\n        status=\"Creating\",\n        progress=\"0%\"\n    )\n    logger.debug(\"Initialized OutputFields\")\n\n    # Check cancellation\n    if extension_manager.is_cancelled():\n        logger.warning(\"Operation cancelled by user\")\n        raise OperationCancelledError(\"User cancelled operation\")\n\n    # Validate resource name\n    logger.info(\"Validating resource name: %s\", input_data.resource_name)\n    try:\n        validate_resource_name(input_data.resource_name)\n        logger.info(\"Resource name validation passed\")\n    except ValidationError as e:\n        logger.error(\"Resource name validation failed: %s\", str(e))\n        raise\n\n    # Update progress\n    output_fields.update(status=\"Validated\", progress=\"25%\")\n\n    # Create resource via API\n    logger.info(\"Creating resource via API: %s\", input_data.resource_name)\n    logger.debug(\"Calling create_resource_api utility\")\n\n    try:\n        resource = create_resource_api(\n            name=input_data.resource_name,\n            timeout=input_data.timeout\n        )\n        logger.info(\"Resource created successfully: %s\", resource.id)\n        logger.debug(\"Resource details: %s\", resource)\n    except APIError as e:\n        logger.error(\"Resource creation failed: %s\", str(e))\n        raise ExecutionError(f\"Failed to create resource: {str(e)}\")\n\n    # Update final status\n    output_fields.update(\n        status=\"Created\",\n        progress=\"100%\"\n    )\n\n    logger.info(\"create_resource action completed successfully\")\n    logger.debug(\"Returning resource_id=%s, resource_name=%s\",\n                 resource.id, resource.name)\n\n    return ActionOutput(\n        resource_id=resource.id,\n        resource_name=resource.name,\n        details={\"status\": \"created\", \"region\": resource.region}\n    )\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Use lazy formatting**: Use `%s` placeholders, not f-strings\n   ```python\n   # Good\n   logger.debug(\"Processing item: %s\", item_id)\n\n   # Bad (f-strings evaluated even if logging disabled)\n   logger.debug(f\"Processing item: {item_id}\")\n   ```\n\n2. **Log at appropriate levels**:\n   - info() - User-facing events\n   - debug() - Developer diagnostic info\n   - warning() - Recoverable issues\n   - error() - Errors (usually followed by raise)\n\n3. **Include context**: Add relevant variable values\n   ```python\n   logger.info(\"Processing batch %d of %d\", current_batch, total_batches)\n   ```\n\n4. **Don't log sensitive data**: Avoid passwords, API keys, tokens\n   ```python\n   # Bad\n   logger.debug(\"API key: %s\", api_key)\n\n   # Good\n   logger.debug(\"API key: %s\", \"***\" if api_key else None)\n   ```\n\n5. **Log exceptions with context**:\n   ```python\n   logger.error(\"Failed to connect to %s: %s\", host, str(e))\n   ```\n\n6. **Module-level logger**: Always use `\"UNV\"`\n   ```python\n   logger = logging.getLogger(\"UNV\")\n   ```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n❌ **Don't log then swallow exceptions**:\n```python\ntry:\n    risky_operation()\nexcept Exception as e:\n    logger.error(\"Error: %s\", str(e))\n    # Missing raise - error is swallowed!\n```\n\n❌ **Don't use print()**: Always use logger\n```python\n# Bad\nprint(\"Processing item\")\n\n# Good\nlogger.info(\"Processing item\")\n```\n\n❌ **Don't log redundant info**:\n```python\n# Bad - extension_manager already logs errors\nextension_manager.add_error(exc)\nlogger.error(\"Error: %s\", exc)  # Redundant\n```\n\n✅ **Do log before raising**:\n```python\nlogger.error(\"Failed to connect: %s\", str(e))\nraise ConnectionError(f\"Connection failed: {str(e)}\")\n```\n\n## Logging Configuration\n\nThe Universal Extension runtime automatically configures logging. You don't need to configure handlers or formatters - just use the logger.\n\nYour logs will appear in:\n- UAC Controller logs\n- Extension task output\n- Standard output (when running locally)\n\nSee `src/extension.py` for base logging configuration.","numLines":364,"startLine":1,"totalLines":364}},"tool_use_id":"toolu_018dGNvQ5uXRHtPuFg41MgY7","duration_ms":3}

