      "content": "# Logging\n\n## Overview\n\nLogging is essential for troubleshooting and debugging Universal Extensions. Use Python's logging module to provide visibility into extension execution.\n\n## Setup\n\n**Import logger at module level:**\n\n```python\nimport logging\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"UNV\")\n```\n\n**ALWAYS use `\"UNV\"` as the logger name** - this ensures all extension logs are captured under the Universal Extension logger hierarchy.\n\n## Logging Levels\n\n### logging.info()\nUse for major steps and important events that should be visible during normal operation:\n\n```python\nlogger.info(\"Starting resource creation\")\nlogger.info(\"Connecting to database: %s\", database_name)\nlogger.info(\"Successfully authenticated with API\")\nlogger.info(\"Completed processing %d items\", total_count)\nlogger.info(\"Action completed successfully\")\n```\n\n**When to use:**\n- Function entry for main operations\n- Connection establishment\n- Authentication success\n- Major milestones (batch processing progress)\n- Successful completion\n\n### logging.debug()\nUse for detailed diagnostic information useful during troubleshooting:\n\n```python\nlogger.debug(\"Request URL: %s\", url)\nlogger.debug(\"Request headers: %s\", headers)\nlogger.debug(\"Response status code: %d\", response.status_code)\nlogger.debug(\"Response data: %s\", response.text)\nlogger.debug(\"Query parameters: %s\", params)\nlogger.debug(\"Processing item: %s\", item_id)\n```\n\n**When to use:**\n- API request/response details\n- Query parameters and payloads\n- Intermediate values and calculations\n- Loop iterations (for debugging)\n- Configuration values\n\n### logging.warning()\nUse for recoverable issues or unexpected situations:\n\n```python\nlogger.warning(\"Retry attempt %d of %d\", attempt, max_retries)\nlogger.warning(\"Item %s skipped: missing required field\", item_id)\nlogger.warning(\"Using default value for %s\", field_name)\n```\n\n### logging.error()\nUse for errors that prevent operation but allow continuation:\n\n```python\nlogger.error(\"Failed to process item %s: %s\", item_id, str(e))\nlogger.error(\"API request failed: %s\", error_message)\n```\n\n**Note**: Errors are typically logged and then raised, not just logged.\n\n## Action Logging Patterns\n\n### Function Entry\n```python\ndef create_resource(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    \"\"\"Create a new resource.\"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Starting create_resource action\")\n    logger.debug(\"Input data: action=%s, resource_name=%s\",\n                 input_data.action, input_data.resource_name)\n```\n\n### Key Operations\n```python\n# Before API call\nlogger.info(\"Creating resource: %s\", resource_name)\nlogger.debug(\"API endpoint: %s\", endpoint_url)\nlogger.debug(\"Request payload: %s\", payload)\n\n# After API call\nlogger.info(\"Resource created successfully: %s\", resource_id)\nlogger.debug(\"API response: %s\", response_data)\n```\n\n### Loop Processing\n```python\nlogger.info(\"Processing %d items\", len(items))\n\nfor i, item in enumerate(items):\n    logger.debug(\"Processing item %d/%d: %s\", i+1, len(items), item.name)\n    # Process item...\n\nlogger.info(\"Completed processing %d items\", len(items))\n```\n\n### Function Exit\n```python\nlogger.info(\"create_resource action completed successfully\")\nlogger.debug(\"Returning resource_id=%s\", resource_id)\nreturn ActionOutput(resource_id=resource_id)\n```\n\n### Error Handling\n```python\ntry:\n    result = risky_operation()\nexcept SpecificError as e:\n    logger.error(\"Operation failed: %s\", str(e))\n    raise ExecutionError(f\"Failed to complete operation: {str(e)}\")\n```\n\n## Utility Function Logging Patterns\n\n### Database Connection\n```python\ndef connect_to_database(host: str, database: str) -> Connection:\n    \"\"\"Connect to PostgreSQL database.\"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Connecting to database: %s@%s\", database, host)\n    logger.debug(\"Connection parameters: host=%s, database=%