"Command failed: {e.stderr}\")\n```\n\n## Complete Example\n\n### Action with Full Logging\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Create resource action.\"\"\"\n\nimport logging\nfrom fields.input import InputFields\nfrom actions.output import ActionOutput\nfrom fields.output import OutputFields\nfrom manager import ExtensionManager\nfrom exceptions import ExecutionError\nfrom utility import create_resource_api, validate_resource_name\n\nlogger = logging.getLogger(\"UNV\")\nextension_manager = ExtensionManager()\n\n\ndef create_resource(input_data: InputFields) -> ActionOutput:\n    \"\"\"\n    Create a new resource.\n\n    Args:\n        input_data: Validated input fields\n\n    Returns:\n        ActionOutput with creation results\n    \"\"\"\n    logger.info(\"Starting create_resource action\")\n    logger.debug(\"Input: action=%s, resource_name=%s, timeout=%s\",\n                 input_data.action,\n                 input_data.resource_name,\n                 input_data.timeout)\n\n    # Initialize output tracking\n    output_fields = OutputFields(\n        status=\"Creating\",\n        progress=\"0%\"\n    )\n    logger.debug(\"Initialized OutputFields\")\n\n    # Check cancellation\n    if extension_manager.is_cancelled():\n        logger.warning(\"Operation cancelled by user\")\n        raise OperationCancelledError(\"User cancelled operation\")\n\n    # Validate resource name\n    logger.info(\"Validating resource name: %s\", input_data.resource_name)\n    try:\n        validate_resource_name(input_data.resource_name)\n        logger.info(\"Resource name validation passed\")\n    except ValidationError as e:\n        logger.error(\"Resource name validation failed: %s\", str(e))\n        raise\n\n    # Update progress\n    output_fields.update(status=\"Validated\", progress=\"25%\")\n\n    # Create resource via API\n    logger.info(\"Creating resource via API: %s\", input_data.resource_name)\n    logger.debug(\"Calling create_resource_api utility\")\n\n    try:\n        resource = create_resource_api(\n            name=input_data.resource_name,\n            timeout=input_data.timeout\n        )\n        logger.info(\"Resource created successfully: %s\", resource.id)\n        logger.debug(\"Resource details: %s\", resource)\n    except APIError as e:\n        logger.error(\"Resource creation failed: %s\", str(e))\n        raise ExecutionError(f\"Failed to create resource: {str(e)}\")\n\n    # Update final status\n    output_fields.update(\n        status=\"Created\",\n        progress=\"100%\"\n    )\n\n    logger.info(\"create_resource action completed successfully\")\n    logger.debug(\"Returning resource_id=%s, resource_name=%s\",\n                 resource.id, resource.name)\n\n    return ActionOutput(\n        resource_id=resource.id,\n        resource_name=resource.name,\n        details={\"status\": \"created\", \"region\": resource.region}\n    )\n```\n\n## Best Practices\n\n1. **Use lazy formatting**: Use `%s` placeholders, not f-strings\n   ```python\n   # Good\n   logger.debug(\"Processing item: %s\", item_id)\n\n   # Bad (f-strings evaluated even if logging disabled)\n   logger.debug(f\"Processing item: {item_id}\")\n   ```\n\n2. **Log at appropriate levels**:\n   - info() - User-facing events\n   - debug() - Developer diagnostic info\n   - warning() - Recoverable issues\n   - error() - Errors (usually followed by raise)\n\n3. **Include context**: Add relevant variable values\n   ```python\n   logger.info(\"Processing batch %d of %d\", current_batch, total_batches)\n   ```\n\n4. **Don't log sensitive data**: Avoid passwords, API keys, tokens\n   ```python\n   # Bad\n   logger.debug(\"API key: %s\", api_key)\n\n   # Good\n   logger.debug(\"API key: %s\", \"***\" if api_key else None)\n   ```\n\n5. **Log exceptions with context**:\n   ```python\n   logger.error(\"Failed to connect to %s: %s\", host, str(e))\n   ```\n\n6. **Module-level logger**: Always use `\"UNV\"`\n   ```python\n   logger = logging.getLogger(\"UNV\")\n   ```\n\n## Common Mistakes\n\n\u274c **Don't log then swallow exceptions**:\n```python\ntry:\n    risky_operation()\nexcept Exception as e:\n    logger.error(\"Error: %s\", str(e))\n    # Missing raise - error is swallowed!\n```\n\n\u274c **Don't use print()**: Always use logger\n```python\n# Bad\nprint(\"Processing item\")\n\n# Good\nlogger.info(\"Processing item\")\n```\n\n\u274c **Don't log redundant info**:\n```python\n# Bad - extension_manager already logs errors\nextension_manager.add_error(exc)\nlogger.error(\"Error: %s\", exc)  # Redundant\n```\n\n\u2705 **Do log before raising**:\n```python\nlogger.error(\"Failed to connect: %s\", str(e))\nraise ConnectionError(f\"Connection failed: {str(e)}\")\n```\n\n## Logging Configuration\n\nThe Universal Extension runtime automatically configures logging. You don't need to configure handlers or formatters - just use the logger.\n\nYour logs will appear in:\n- UAC Controller logs\n- Extension task output\n- Standard output (when running locally)\n\nSee `src/extension.py` for base logging configuration.",
